    "VISUAL_NAME": "Pie",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_ASSET_VERIFICATION_COVERAGE_PIE",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "Asset Verification Coverage by Category (Pie). Slices = Asset Category (FAM_ASSET_CATEGORY_MASTER.CATEGORY_NAME), value = VERIFIED_ASSETS = count of distinct in-service assets (FAM_ASSET_REGISTER.STATUS='ACTIVE') in that category that have at least one FAM_PHYSICAL_VERIFICATION_LINE row with a non-null VERIFIED_DATE inside the selected period (>= the Verification Period From prompt, <= CURRENT_DATE) - so the pie shows each category's share of verified assets, mirroring the VERIFIED_ASSETS measure of the sibling Grid visual fam_asset_verification_coverage. Same two criteria as that Grid visual are kept: an optional Asset Category filter (like + '%' default, lookup to FAM_ASSET_CATEGORY_MASTER) and the Verification Period From date prompt (default 12 months before today). Categories with zero verified assets in the period still appear as a (zero-value) slice via the LEFT JOIN, since the underlying Grid visual lists all categories. This is a SEPARATE visual object from fam_asset_verification_coverage (which stays a Grid and is already published to the app menu) so the pie can be added to the Management Dashboard without disturbing the existing menu item.",
